{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman","id":563473,"title":"What are the Huntsmen/Huntsman?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-21T16:14:39-07:00","id":563473,"title":"What are the Huntsmen/Huntsman?","content":"Okay, I've seen several refrences to the Huntsmen/man but has it been revealed as to exactly what they/it/him/her are? are there more than one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:20:13-07:00","id":563506,"title":"","content":"There are more than one, <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">the outline talks about them somewhat</a>, and beyond that, the only ones who know the details about them are people involved with writing Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:30:10-07:00","id":563511,"title":"","content":"Huntsmen are a new antagonist that will be debuting in 2nd edition, filling a similar role in the chronicle as Strix fill for vampires and Idigam fill for werewolves. We don't know much about them yet, except that they are free agents who work for the Gentry to track down and recapture escaped changelings. From what we've heard, they will have some ability to change their appearance, or possibly shapeshift, into just about anything. They can also use Icons, bits of a Changeling that she leaves behind in her escape, in order to track the changeling no matter where she goes. In a very literal sense, you can run but you can't hide from a Huntsman with your Icon. But, the Icon can only last so long outside of the hedge, and eventually deteriorates and reforms where the changeling it is linked to first left it. We know that they will be truly formidable antagonists, but more because of their ability as hunters than their combat prowess. They're scary because they can find you anywhere and be anything, not because they beat face. We know that Courts use things called Approaches, which give Huntsmen some kind of advantage called Yearning if they go after the court's members on their own terms (for example, going after an Autumn Courtier in her dreams), and we know that Mantle can give individual characters their own personal Approaches. But we don't know what Yearning does yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T17:28:51-07:00","id":563572,"title":"","content":"I assume that its somehow related to the Huntsman in the 1e Changeling core. Same concept as that antagonist, but much more immediate and relevant to the day to day operation of most freeholds.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T23:14:17-07:00","id":565052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=563511#post563511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen are a new antagonist that will be debuting in 2nd edition, filling a similar role in the chronicle as Strix fill for vampires and Idigam fill for werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because this has been misunderstood many times before, I want to elaborate on this statement.<br /> <br /> &quot;Antagonists&quot; doesn't really do justice to the essence of what these title-figures are. The devs have used the phrase &quot;story catalysts&quot;, but I'd describe them as the things that upset the story cart. You have a number of fairly standard stories for each game line. Into each of these, you can throw the title-figure: the Strix, the Huntsmen, the Idigam, the Fallen World, the Firestorm: and suddenly things skew sideways. The story isn't the same story anymore. A changeling story is about figuring out how to reassemble a self-image, trying to make the broken glass shards fit despite suffering from echoes of trauma. Into this, the Huntsman is about spiking your paranoia, exploiting your successes, risking all your psychological comfort. The original story is broken; you either force it back or you let it unravel and see where that takes you.<br /> <br /> Imagine a story where you hear about a Huntsman in the Hedge. You do some research and realize the target isn't in your motley; he's an NPC. And he's succumbing (or however that works), on the verge of being snatched. It's a race against time! You have to find the Huntsman and murderize it first! And you do get there in time. And... you fall in love. And that love is requited, and... nothing. It decides to stop Hunting, because of the effort you put in, whyever and however its original reasons, how you convince it to do so, etc., etc. There's no betrayal of trust where it makes off with you towards Arcadia; it even seeks out ways to recompense. Sure, there are hitches; disbelief, distrust, and dismay from fellow Lost. But... is that really an antagonist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T23:51:13-07:00","id":565064,"title":"","content":"One of the biggest shortcomings of 1e Changlling is it's lack of clear motivations for threats that Changelings face.<br /> The biggest threat being Fairies. They make a great example. Their motivations range from obsession, to the lazy boredom. As a nemesis this makes them foreboding and mysterious. But at a ground level of design, Are they really the most apparent threat too a Changeling? Gentry could want ANYTHING. Sur,e they might be presenting themselves a physical threat. But is could all just be ruse to test the Lost for some mad motivation.<br /> A good chunk of the supplements were spent defining ways Gentry were limited in scope to be actual threats a Changelings to could best.<br /> Meanwhile. Huntsmen existed in core but were never elaborated on. There is the Great Hunt. Bun no defined way it affected anything.<br /> <br /> So what are the Huntsmen now? A clear Threat with a clear Motive. It isn't just toying with the fae on a whim of fantsy. It is going to take them down. It's goal is to defeat it's target.<br /> <br /> Of all of the Threats in Changeling. It is easiest to understand the Hunters and easiest to motivate a rally-cry against them. Gentry might be reasoned with. Huntsmen are not. Hobs migh be misunderstood. Huntsmen are not. Human's might just be ignorant cat's paws. Huntsmen are not. Fetches might just be bystanders. Huntsmen are not.<br /> <br /> Another shortcoming of 1e was that the Hedge is too forgiving. It has the danger level mostly right. But the danger only lasted as long as you remained inside the Hedge. Huntsmen seem to fill a need to make traversing the Hedge an unknowable risk long after you leave said Hedge. It's not just what you leave behind, but also who might find what you left behind.<br /> <br /> I am eager to read the full depth of development behind the Huntsmen and how they relate to the Gentry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T09:50:51-07:00","id":565500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=565052#post565052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this has been misunderstood many times before, I want to elaborate on this statement.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Antagonists&amp;quot; doesn't really do justice to the essence of what these title-figures are. The devs have used the phrase &amp;quot;story catalysts&amp;quot;, but I'd describe them as the things that upset the story cart. You have a number of fairly standard stories for each game line. Into each of these, you can throw the title-figure: the Strix, the Huntsmen, the Idigam, the Fallen World, the Firestorm: and suddenly things skew sideways. The story isn't the same story anymore. A changeling story is about figuring out how to reassemble a self-image, trying to make the broken glass shards fit despite suffering from echoes of trauma. Into this, the Huntsman is about spiking your paranoia, exploiting your successes, risking all your psychological comfort. The original story is broken; you either force it back or you let it unravel and see where that takes you.<br /> <br /> Imagine a story where you hear about a Huntsman in the Hedge. You do some research and realize the target isn't in your motley; he's an NPC. And he's succumbing (or however that works), on the verge of being snatched. It's a race against time! You have to find the Huntsman and murderize it first! And you do get there in time. And... you fall in love. And that love is requited, and... nothing. It decides to stop Hunting, because of the effort you put in, whyever and however its original reasons, how you convince it to do so, etc., etc. There's no betrayal of trust where it makes off with you towards Arcadia; it even seeks out ways to recompense. Sure, there are hitches; disbelief, distrust, and dismay from fellow Lost. But... is that really an antagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like any well-written antagonist should do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:21:12-07:00","id":566580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=565500#post565500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like any well-written antagonist should do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>/shrug<br /> <br /> You may as well say that any well-written character should do this. It's just as true, and just as pointless a statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:43:35-07:00","id":566676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=566580#post566580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">/shrug<br /> <br /> You may as well say that any well-written character should do this. It's just as true, and just as pointless a statement.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, you're now saying everything you wrote about title characters above is pointless?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:18:40-07:00","id":566710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=566676#post566676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, you're now saying everything you wrote about title characters above is pointless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not do this song and dance.<br /> <br /> It is possible for a well-written antagonist to nevertheless be something that doesn't shake up the status quo of the average game \u2014 spirits are generally this in Werewolf, as are ghosts in Geist and the Machine in Demon, because they're a constantly-happening background concern in a given typical locale rather than an unknown quantity of enigmatic provenance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:22:24-07:00","id":566717,"title":"","content":"I hope they turn out to be kind of like an anti-changeling or something. That'd be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:40:13-07:00","id":566814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=566710#post566710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not do this song and dance.<br /> <br /> It is possible for a well-written antagonist to nevertheless be something that doesn't shake up the status quo of the average game \u2014 spirits are generally this in Werewolf, as are ghosts in Geist and the Machine in Demon, because they're a constantly-happening background concern in a given typical locale rather than an unknown quantity of enigmatic provenance.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same token though, it is possible for a Strix or an Idigam to not shake up the status quo of the average game. Just because they're titular antagonists doesn't mean they're above being called antagonists. I don't think Errol was wrong, these antagonists are certainly meant to be story catalysts, at least within the context of the chronicles that are named after them. It's just that they can also easily not be, and other antagonists can easily fill the same role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:15:03-07:00","id":566838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=566710#post566710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not do this song and dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awwwww.... .but they're totally playing my tune! <br /> <br /> Okay, serious time. The titular characters are supposed to be some kind of &quot;out of context&quot; issue that does change things. It doesn't have to be an antagonist, remember! With Mage, we've got the Fallen World Chronicles. Promethean is the Firestorm Chronicles. Hells, even Idigam don't have to be antagonistic.<br /> <br /> So, the entire approach of looking at titular characters as antagonists in the first place is flawed. Yes, strix and huntsmen are antagonists, but that's not a rule. So, we should be looking at this from another angle entirely. <br /> <br /> Now, assuming that Fallen World is actually refering to paradox effects, these titlular things are what the games designed to challenge the status quo. Or call it a story catalyst, or upsetting the apple cart. The point is that, in general, we have context and situations in place for handling the usual. Invictus elder getting power grabby, or the Brood and VII come to town? We got ways of dealing with it. The five sacred prey? We know how to hunt them. The Gentry, we have methods. Seers, banishes, liches, scelesti, ephemeral foes? Pick your arcana. The titular events (and, even if we're talking people, their arrival is an event) are out of context. Its something that you can't really prepare for. It throws everything into chaos. Even if something else could serve, these titular events are designed to work that way, while the others are not. That's why they get the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T21:27:12-07:00","id":567355,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Ok, I'll buy that. Thank you for the insight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T21:36:18-07:00","id":567361,"title":"","content":"This is only me being slightly cheeky.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Huntsman_spider_with_meal.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T21:43:49-07:00","id":567378,"title":"","content":"My mother in law?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T00:14:51-07:00","id":567493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=566838#post566838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, assuming that Fallen World is actually refering to paradox effects, these titlular things are what the games designed to challenge the status quo. Or call it a story catalyst, or upsetting the apple cart. The point is that, in general, we have context and situations in place for handling the usual. Invictus elder getting power grabby, or the Brood and VII come to town? We got ways of dealing with it. The five sacred prey? We know how to hunt them. The Gentry, we have methods. Seers, banishes, liches, scelesti, ephemeral foes? Pick your arcana. The titular events (and, even if we're talking people, their arrival is an event) are out of context. Its something that you can't really prepare for. It throws everything into chaos. Even if something else could serve, these titular events are designed to work that way, while the others are not. That's why they get the title.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fallen World is refering to the Mysteries the Awakened dwell in their lives. You have your typical setting of Pentacle, Seers and others - and then BAM, the angel fell from the sky. The reality wormhole is open. Time self repeating room is discovered. Ancient living statues of blue visitors are uncovered. And now whole mage community is changed and goes out to fight and hunt for this new Mystery, Or at least this is kind sound from previews.<br /> <br /> I say that Huntman are central antagonists/catalyst points as they &quot;speed up the setting&quot;. Previous you had rather static Courts system - now it's based to dwell in to Approaches against Huntsman. Previous True Fae were distant antagonistic gods showing maybe once or twice in chronicle - now they have Huntmans as that are day-to-day threat to the Freehold ( well, maybe week-to-month rather ). Much more story dynamic added by they existence in the setting - just like with the Strix, Idigam and Mysteries of Vampire, Werewolf and Mage, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:38:21-07:00","id":567639,"title":"","content":"I have two main theories for the Huntsmen at this point. One is stronger than the other, but the other is by far cooler.<br /> <br /> The first: The Huntsmen are a variety of creatures from Faerie that are (like all non-True Fae in Arcadia) servants to the Gentry. I believe they will be somewhat like foils to the Changelings they hunt in that regard because they're not beholden to the Wyrd laws that prohibit the Kindly Folk from just plucking their escaped slaves back with the similar ease at which they captured them to begin with (as hinted abount in the Freehold Article and in the mechanic involving a Changeling's Mantle being added to their Defense against the True Fae specifically) or are able to bypass them utilizing loopholes similar to the one's Changelings use in order to draw upon Contract's and Pledges (A sort of <i>not human but less than a True Fae</i> kinda thing.)<br /> <br /> The second: The Huntsmen is the seventh Seeming and will play a sort of Deceived-esc role in Changeling 2e. While this would be super cool I feel it's the weaker argument since this would essentially make Loyalists completly arbitrary and the main reason this theory is here is because it was said that the seventh Seeming will be released in a later supplement and despite how cool the new take on Seemings are it still wouldn't be more than a footnote unless it was the main focus of the suplement (ala Book of the Deceived)<br /> <br /> Actually thinking about it now it would make more sense to just make Loyalists the seventh Seeming since they would have to either rip out their heart and give it willingly to their Keeper or they wouldn't have a Seeming at all since they never truly escaped Arcadia. So nvm, my money's on the first theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T05:16:52-07:00","id":567709,"title":"","content":"I think Huntsmen are Hobgoblins with the Huntsmen's Template added. And I think Yearning is something a Huntsmen can spend to block the protection of the Bulwark granted to Changelings. So if a Huntsmen spends a point of yearning for say a scene the Changeling can no longer apply his mantle to his rolls when dealing with a Huntsmen. So if a Huntsmen is foolish enough to attack a Changeling without using an Approach, the Changeling can use the full power of they're mantle against the Huntsmen as a servant of the True Fae, making the Changeling far more dangerous to the Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> Just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T20:07:19-07:00","id":573491,"title":"","content":"What if Huntsmen not only use but are made from the changeling's Icon? <br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be scary to have a being made from a piece of your soul hunt you? Like some sort of weird doppleganger but native to Arcadia. <br /> <br /> It would explain why they are so good at finding a specific changeling...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T20:13:23-07:00","id":573492,"title":"","content":"Funnily, I hit on the same sort of ideas recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T00:45:08-07:00","id":574868,"title":"","content":"Can a Huntman say &quot;Nope, I don't wanna use the Yearning your Court oh-so kindly offer, but to engage you in my own terms &quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T08:59:37-07:00","id":575284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=574868#post574868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Huntman say &quot;Nope, I don't wanna use the Yearning your Court oh-so kindly offer, but to engage you in my own terms &quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the sound of it, a Huntsman doesn't have to follow the Court's Approaches, but the wording suggests that it's uncommon. (emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Court Creation</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abiding Autumn's Approach, a Huntsman <b>is not likely</b> to challenge her to a duel with pistols or ambush her in the dark and drag her off by force. Instead, the Huntsman may torment her in her dreams before challenging her to a mystical duel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever Yearning does, it's clearly a big incentive. There may well be others in the Huntsman writeup, when we see it. Perhaps there's a stick to match the carrot, and a Huntsman is penalized for going after a Changeling in a Court when not using the right Approach. Regardless, I expect that if a Huntsman's reward is big enough to make up for not gaining any Yearning (and to make up for any other downsides to eschewing an approach), she'd take the job.<br /> <br /> More often, though, I expect the Gentry wouldn't just seek out any generic Huntsman, and not just any Huntsman would step forward. They'd probably try to align skillsets to the job, so that even when following the Court's Approach, the Huntsman <i>is</i> engaging on her own terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T07:50:38-07:00","id":576356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>De_K47</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=573491#post573491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Huntsmen not only use but are made from the changeling's Icon?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be scary to have a being made from a piece of your soul hunt you? Like some sort of weird doppleganger but native to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> It would explain why they are so good at finding a specific changeling...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, that's a cool idea. Kind of like a reverse Fetch. Or the like the Arcadian version of a Fetch. What if a Changeling's Fetch wasn't something left behind by the Keeper when they snatch a Changeling, but rather reality's (or the God Machine's) reaction to the hole left by the Changeling being taken? What if Arcadia had a similar reaction when the Changeling escapes?<br /> <br /> I'm going to be using this idea in a game regardless if it is at all accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:37:15-07:00","id":580936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/563473-what-are-the-huntsmen-huntsman?p=567361#post567361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only me being slightly cheeky.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> SOOOOO much fucking NOPE!<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> By the way, I had an idea: What if Loyalists with Seemings are those who escaped but got captured again and had their minds reprogrammed by their angry Keepers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-06-2015, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}